    }
  }
  return false;
}
```

vs waitForOutput — identical loop, differing only in `break`+return buffer vs `return true/false`. True duplication (~15 lines). The doc even says "Same stability rule as [waitForOutput]". If the stability rule changes (e.g. turns or deadline semantics), two places to update. SUGGESTION: extract the shared loop.

Another subtle behavior: in `liveWaitForScreen` with settle, each poll iteration that matches re-runs `waitForRawSettle` — with the 2s grace cap. If the CLI stalls mid-frame and NEVER finishes within 2s of the match... then settled screen may still lack item rows; pattern check fails; loop continues; next match re-settles. Total time bounded by `timeout` (15s here). Good.

Edge: `waitForRawSettle` grace of 2s with the deadline checked at loop top; a `settleMs: 200` delay can overshoot deadline by 200ms max. Fine.

